      "writtenOn": "2022-07-15T17:13:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like `libjpeg-turbo` itself would use [`WARNMS`](https://source.corp.google.com/android-internal/external/libjpeg-turbo/jerror.h;l\u003d276?q\u003dWARNMS\u0026ct\u003dos\u0026sq\u003dpackage:%5Eandroid-internal$%20-file:external%2Fskqp%20-file:external%2Fqt).\n\nPersonally, I don\u0027t think it\u0027s absolutely necessary. Most users don\u0027t care about this information - they just want to see the image. And if it showed an image somewhere else, but not on Android, that looks broken.\n\nUsing `SkCodecPrintf` seems fine - it gives a little information if they\u0027re looking for it - meaning they\u0027ve set the compile flag so that `SkCodecPrintf` actually prints anything. (By default, it\u0027s skipped.)\n\nA little history behind `SkCodecPrintf` - we added it because people on Android were asking for more information about why decodes failed. It\u0027s activated with a flag, because it can be noisy. But AFAIK, no one is building with it turned on anymore - it ended up being noisy on Android, and just resulted in bugs being assigned to me even though they were unrelated.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 67,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 67,
        "endChar": 108
      },
